    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for mutt",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for mutt fixes the following issues\n\n- CVE-2026-43859: `strfcpy` used instead of `memcpy` for the IMAP `auth_cram` MD5 digest (bsc#1263897).\n- CVE-2026-43860: truncation of `hash_passwd` by one byte for IMAP `auth_cram` MD5 digest (bsc#1263896).\n- CVE-2026-43861: missing check for `\\0` in `url_pct_decode` (bsc#1263895).\n- CVE-2026-43862: mishandling of the `imap_auth_gss` security level (bsc#1263894).\n- CVE-2026-43863: infinite loop in `data_object_to_stream` in `crypt-gpgme.c` (bsc#1263893).\n- CVE-2026-43864: NULL pointer dereference in function `show_sig_summary` (bsc#1263892).\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "openSUSE-Leap-16.0-1028",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
